WEBVTT

00:00:00.556 --> 00:00:03.386
Cryptography is the art of hiding meaning.

00:00:04.006 --> 00:00:08.576
It turns a readable message into
something unreadable, and back again.

00:00:10.256 --> 00:00:14.546
Plaintext is the original
intelligible message or data.

00:00:15.076 --> 00:00:17.006
It is what you want to protect.

00:00:18.829 --> 00:00:22.879
Ciphertext is the transformed,
unintelligible form.

00:00:23.379 --> 00:00:26.289
An attacker who sees it
learns nothing useful.

00:00:28.022 --> 00:00:31.232
Encryption turns
plaintext into ciphertext.

00:00:31.677 --> 00:00:35.067
Decryption turns ciphertext
back into plaintext.

00:00:35.592 --> 00:00:37.422
The same process in reverse.

00:00:39.322 --> 00:00:42.632
A cipher is the algorithm
for the transformation.

00:00:43.247 --> 00:00:47.337
A cryptosystem adds key
management and key distribution.

00:00:47.932 --> 00:00:50.382
The algorithm alone is not enough.

00:00:52.089 --> 00:00:54.419
A key controls the transformation.

00:00:55.004 --> 00:00:57.074
It is the input to the algorithm.

00:00:57.739 --> 00:01:00.689
Key space is the set of all possible keys.

00:01:01.309 --> 00:01:04.279
A larger key space means a stronger lock.

00:01:05.956 --> 00:01:07.126
A simple example:

00:01:07.536 --> 00:01:10.606
replace each letter with
the one three places later.

00:01:11.161 --> 00:01:13.111
Meet becomes phhw.

00:01:13.726 --> 00:01:16.876
That is a substitution
cipher with key three.

00:01:18.556 --> 00:01:22.166
Plaintext, ciphertext,
cipher, key, key space.

00:01:22.781 --> 00:01:27.331
These five words are the foundation
of every algorithm that follows.

